 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "bosch 24 not draining, water sitting in bottom. help"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Before you start, switch it off and unplug it. I cannot provide specific repair steps without knowing the exact model number and any error codes displayed. Please check your appliance for a code or look at the rating plate to identify the precise model, then ask a more detailed question about that fault. From what you have described, the most likely cause is drain filter (twist out and clean - first thing). Take out the lower rack, then twist and lift out the filter in the bottom of the tub. Rinse it under the tap and clear any food, grease or glass from the sump underneath. Was the filter or sump blocked (and is it clean now), or was it already clean?\n[Helpful to see: image \"Where the filter is\" — The filter sits in the base of the dishwasher, usually under the bottom spray arm. Twist it out anticlockwise and rinse it under a tap. Typical layout — your dishwasher may differ.]"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "model is SMS24AW01G. E:24 on display. filter was blocked, food and bit of broken glass. gloves on. cleaned it, drains fine now, E:24 gone"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Good news, that has sorted it. If it happens again, start with the same check. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  }
 ],
